<title>BRAZIL: Brazil's CMN approves Banerj selloff plan.</title>
<headline>Brazil's CMN approves Banerj selloff plan.</headline>
<dateline>BRASILIA 1996-09-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Brazil's National Monetary Council approved a plan to privatize Banerj, a bank owned by Rio de Janeiro state, a senior government official said.</p>
<p>The CMN, the Brazilian government's most senior monetary policy body, recommended the bank be privatized by the end of 1996, Central Bank director Alkimar Moura told reporters.</p>
<p>Moura also said the CMN would recommend that no limit be placed foreign investors seeking to buy into the institution.</p>
</text>
